    <Placemark>
      <name>Champ Grande</name>
      <styleUrl>#arch</styleUrl>
      <description><![CDATA[<div style="font:13px/1.45 Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:400px"><table><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Site</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Champ Grande</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Country</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">France</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Entry type</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Archaeological</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Species attribution</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">H. neanderthalensis</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Technology (interpreted)</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Other</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Age</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">71 - 50 ka</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Basis for date</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Slimak pers. comm. According to geological analyis.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Scope of entry</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Single sequence</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Technology described</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Blades relying on initial shape of cobble with natural dihedral corner. shaping is slight some cresting to form corner better. Examples in fig. 8. 2 3 4. facetting performed. some bipolar percussion Slimak suggests is used to maintain distal convexity. Cautious in describing tablets as present. So no tablets. Soft hammer seems maybe but they don't say for sure present as far as I can tell.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Published source</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Slimak 1999</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Techniques recorded</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">10 of 33</td></tr></table><p style="margin:10px 0 3px"><b>Procedural units present</b></p><p style="margin:0">Platform faceting, Distal shaping, Cresting, Hard hammer percussion, Support core with hand, Core rotation, Soft hammer percussion, Invasive flaking, Retouch, Burination</p></div>]]></description>
