      <description><![CDATA[<div style="font:13px/1.45 Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:400px"><table><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Site</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Itinnera</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Country</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Greenland</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Entry type</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Archaeological</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Species attribution</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">H. sapiens</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Technology (interpreted)</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Other</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Age</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">4.4 - 3 ka</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Basis for date</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">-</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Scope of entry</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Single sequence</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Technology described</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Arctic small tool tradition at Saqqaq. Burins made on little bifaces. hafted. burin spalls taken through pressure.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Published source</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">Sorensen 2004</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 10px 2px 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><b>Techniques recorded</b></td><td style="padding:2px 0">10 of 33</td></tr></table><p style="margin:10px 0 3px"><b>Procedural units present</b></p><p style="margin:0">Back shaping, Abrasion, Hard hammer percussion, Support core with hand, Core rotation, Burination, Tanging, Bifacial retouch, Invasive retouch, Pressure flaked retouch</p></div>]]></description>
